{"id":"93df685cc0032d09","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-thm-banach-tarski.md","title":"Banach-Tarski Paradox","display":"thm-banach-tarski — Banach-Tarski Paradox","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-banach-tarski","aliases":["58-thm-banach-tarski","Banach-Tarski Paradox","Banach-Tarski Decomposition"],"display":"thm-banach-tarski — Banach-Tarski Paradox","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","[[../batch18/58-thm-zorn.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-isometry.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-bijective.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-banach-tarski"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-banach-tarski</span><span>Banach-Tarski Paradox</span><span>Banach-Tarski Decomposition</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-banach-tarski — Banach-Tarski Paradox"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2830b5df14164544\" href=\"?note=2830b5df14164544\" title=\"../batch18/58-thm-zorn.md\">../batch18/58-thm-zorn.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"cd1b4dafb5eb0840\" href=\"?note=cd1b4dafb5eb0840\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-isometry.md\">../batch13/58-df-isometry.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md\">../batch18/58-df-bijective.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^3 : \\sum_{k&lt;3}x_k^2\\le 1\\}\">\\(B = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^3 : \\sum_{k&lt;3}x_k^2\\le 1\\}\\)</span> (unit ball, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}^3\">\\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\)</span> (three-dimensional Euclidean space, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\">\\(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\)</span> is the Euclidean isometry predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\)</span> requires the rigid motion to be onto</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}banach\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\nB=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:\\sum_{k&lt;3}x_k^2\\leq1\\}\\to\n\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\exists(A_i)_{i&lt;m}\\;\\exists(C_j)_{j&lt;n}\\;\n\\exists(g_i)_{i&lt;m}\\;\\exists(h_j)_{j&lt;n}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\n\\Bigl(\nB=\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{i&lt;m}A_i\\Bigr)\n\\sqcup\n\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{j&lt;n}C_j\\Bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall i&lt;m\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall j&lt;n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{i&lt;m}g_i[A_i]\n\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{j&lt;n}h_j[C_j]\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}banach\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\nB=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:\\sum_{k&lt;3}x_k^2\\leq1\\}\\to\n\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\exists(A_i)_{i&lt;m}\\;\\exists(C_j)_{j&lt;n}\\;\n\\exists(g_i)_{i&lt;m}\\;\\exists(h_j)_{j&lt;n}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\n\\Bigl(\nB=\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{i&lt;m}A_i\\Bigr)\n\\sqcup\n\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{j&lt;n}C_j\\Bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall i&lt;m\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall j&lt;n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{i&lt;m}g_i[A_i]\n\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{j&lt;n}h_j[C_j]\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Banach and Tarski (1924): proved the paradox.</li>\n<li>Hausdorff (1914): earlier related paradox for sphere.</li>\n<li>The decomposition uses finitely many pieces moved by rigid motions.</li>\n<li>The construction depends on choice and fails in amenable settings.</li>\n<li>The pieces of the original ball are split into two disjoint groups; each group is moved and reassembled into a full unit ball.</li>\n<li>Demonstrates &quot;cost&quot; of AC: non-measurable sets necessary.</li>\n<li>Solovay (1970): model where all sets measurable, paradox fails.</li>\n<li>Not a true &quot;paradox&quot;: logically consistent, just counterintuitive.</li>\n<li>Applications: understanding limits of measure theory, amenability theory.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-thm-zorn.md","status":"resolved","id":"2830b5df14164544","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-zorn.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-isometry.md","status":"resolved","id":"cd1b4dafb5eb0840","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-isometry.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-bijective.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$B = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^3 : \\sum_{k<3}x_k^2\\le 1\\}$ (unit ball, see [[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathbb{R}^3$ (three-dimensional Euclidean space, see [[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"B = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^3 : \\sum_{k<3}x_k^2\\le 1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{R}^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Bijective}(g,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}banach\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\nB=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:\\sum_{k<3}x_k^2\\leq1\\}\\to\n\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\n\\exists(A_i)_{i<m}\\;\\exists(C_j)_{j<n}\\;\n\\exists(g_i)_{i<m}\\;\\exists(h_j)_{j<n}\\;\\\\\n&\\quad\n\\Bigl(\nB=\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{i<m}A_i\\Bigr)\n\\sqcup\n\\Bigl(\\bigsqcup_{j<n}C_j\\Bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall i<m\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(g_i,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\n\\land\n\\forall j<n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Isometry}_S(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(h_j,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb R^3)\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{i<m}g_i[A_i]\n\\land\nB=\\bigsqcup_{j<n}h_j[C_j]\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":2203,"backlinks":[{"id":"90ebdc5f6dcdaf9b","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4042","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-thm-banach-tarski.md|58-thm-banach-tarski]]（batch08）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-149","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md]]\n[[58-thm-ac-wellorder-equivalent.md]]\n[[58-thm-aleph-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-completeness.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category-theory.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category.md]]\n[[58-thm-banach-tarski.md]]\n[[58-thm-beth-function-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-boolean-valued-model.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-determinacy-proof.md]]\n[[58-thm-bounded-forcing-axioms.md]]\n[[58-thm-cantor.md]]\n[[58-thm-cardinal-multiplication.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-filter-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-guessing.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection-proper.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection.md]]\n[[58-thm-coanalytic-separation.md]]\n[[58-thm-coding-universe.md]]\n[[58-thm-cofinality-regular.md]]\n[[58-thm-cohen-forcing-CH.md]]\n[[58-thm-collapse-forcing.md]]\n[[58-thm-compactness.md]]\n[[58-thm-consistency-strength-hierarchy.md]]\n[[58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]]\n[[58-thm-countable-choice.md]]\n[[58-thm-covering-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dense-set-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dependent-choic